            <ArticleTitle>OP-19 APPLICABILITY OF THE ROME III CRITERIA IN CHILDREN PRESENTED WITH RECURRENT ABDOMINAL PAIN FOR A RANDOMIZED CONTROLLED GROUP INTERVENTIONAL STUDY.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>517</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.mpg.0000472223.09292.f0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">&lt;AT&gt;</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">&lt;/AT&gt; Functional abdominal pain (FAP) according to the paediatric ROME III (pRIII) criteria appears to be highly prevalent among school children. The differentiation between organic and functional abdominal pain is a challenge. Indeed, the capacity of the pRIII criteria to identify patients with FAP is still debated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
